{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the distance between the foci of the hyperbola given by the equation \\(\\frac{x^2}{50} - \\frac{y^2}{22} = 2\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Rewrite the equation in the standard form of a hyperbola.\n2. Identify the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n3. Calculate the distance between the foci using the relationship \\(c^2 = a^2 + b^2\\).\n\n### Step 1: Rewrite the equation in standard form\n\nThe given equation is \\(\\frac{x^2}{50} - \\frac{y^2}{22} = 2\\). To convert this into the standard form, we divide every term by 2:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{100} - \\frac{y^2}{44} = 1\n\\]\n\nThis is now in the standard form of a hyperbola \\(\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\\), where \\(a^2 = 100\\) and \\(b^2 = 44\\).\n\n","prefix_end":698,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,6010,1948,279,282,2119,315,279,17071,65,7924,2661,553,279,23606,1124,11520,37018,45340,61,17,15170,20,15,92,481,1124,37018,90,88,61,17,15170,17,17,92,284,220,17,59,701,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,93213,279,23606,304,279,5297,1352,315,264,17071,65,7924,624,17,13,64547,279,2750,315,17767,64,57758,323,17767,65,59,4292,18,13,20517,279,6010,1948,279,282,2119,1667,279,5025,17767,66,61,17,284,264,61,17,488,293,61,17,59,3593,14374,14822,220,16,25,93213,279,23606,304,5297,1352,271,785,2661,23606,374,1124,11520,37018,45340,61,17,15170,20,15,92,481,1124,37018,90,88,61,17,15170,17,17,92,284,220,17,59,568,2014,5508,419,1119,279,5297,1352,11,582,21749,1449,4647,553,220,17,1447,59,9640,59,37018,45340,61,17,15170,16,15,15,92,481,1124,37018,90,88,61,17,15170,19,19,92,284,220,16,198,59,2533,1986,374,1431,304,279,5297,1352,315,264,17071,65,7924,1124,11520,37018,45340,61,17,15170,64,61,17,92,481,1124,37018,90,88,61,17,15170,65,61,17,92,284,220,16,59,701,1380,17767,64,61,17,284,220,16,15,15,57758,323,17767,65,61,17,284,220,19,19,